  "id": "boe_bororo_funeral_song",
  "name": "Boe (Bororo) funeral and ritual song",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ritual song of the Boe (Bororo) of central Mato Grosso, whose funeral cycle runs for weeks or months after a death, with nightly singing in the village plaza and men's house led by ritual song specialists. Groups of men answer a leading singer while shaking large gourd rattles (bapo), and in the funeral rites whirled bull-roarers give voice to the aije spirits. The Salesian missionaries César Albisetti and Ângelo Jayme Venturelli documented songs and rites in the Enciclopédia Bororo, and ethnographers have since recorded the funeral song cycles.",
  "recipe": "classic modern boe (bororo) funeral and ritual song, ritual Devotional, indigenous branch. traditional gourd calabash maracas, large slat slow whirl ritual summoning bullroarer. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
